<section class="mission methodology-section">
  <p class="eyebrow">THE CAL METHOD</p>

  <h2>Design. Build. Validate. Publish.</h2>

  <p class="section-intro">
    Cloud Architect Lab uses a repeatable engineering lifecycle to transform
    technical learning into practical architecture case studies.
  </p>

  <div class="methodology-grid">
    <article class="methodology-card">
      <span class="methodology-number">01</span>
      <h3>Design</h3>
      <p>
        Define requirements, constraints, trust boundaries, architecture,
        technical decisions, and success criteria before implementation.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="methodology-card">
      <span class="methodology-number">02</span>
      <h3>Build</h3>
      <p>
        Implement the approved design using Infrastructure as Code, reusable
        modules, version control, and clearly separated engineering concerns.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="methodology-card">
      <span class="methodology-number">03</span>
      <h3>Validate</h3>
      <p>
        Compare the deployed environment with the documented architecture,
        verify expected behavior, and capture evidence before making claims.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="methodology-card">
      <span class="methodology-number">04</span>
      <h3>Publish</h3>
      <p>
        Share the architecture, implementation, decisions, tradeoffs,
        validation results, and lessons that should influence future designs.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="principles">
    <div>
      <strong>Architecture before implementation</strong>
      <p>Design intent guides the code—not the other way around.</p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <strong>Evidence before claims</strong>
      <p>Validation demonstrates that the deployed system matches the design.</p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <strong>Lessons carried forward</strong>
      <p>Every case study improves the standards used by the next one.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>